{"name":"Shire","hex":"#646b59","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Shire","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname.","A placename.\n  A river in Malawi and Mozambique"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A breed of draught horse; an individual of this breed."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Shire"}],"entries":[{"title":"Shire","blocks":[{"text":"Shire is a traditional term for an administrative division of land in Great Britain and some other English-speaking and Commonwealth countries. It is generally synonymous with county. English counties are among the oldest extant national divisions in the world."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Three_Shire.jpg/330px-Three_Shire.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shire","wikidata":"Q662296"},{"title":"Shire (pharmaceutical company)","blocks":[{"text":"Shire plc was a UK-founded Jersey-registered specialty biopharmaceutical company. Originating in the United Kingdom with an operational base in the United States, its brands and products included Vyvanse, Lialda, and Adderall XR. Shire was acquired by Takeda Pharmaceutical Company on 8 January 2019."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shire_(pharmaceutical_company)","wikidata":"Q905049"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Anglo-Saxon_Chronicle_-_scire_%28British_Library_Cotton_MS_Tiberius_A_VI%2C_folio_11v%29.jpg/250px-Anglo-Saxon_Chronicle_-_scire_%28British_Library_Cotton_MS_Tiberius_A_VI%2C_folio_11v%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/3c/Anglo-Saxon_Chronicle_-_scire_%28British_Library_Cotton_MS_Tiberius_A_VI%2C_folio_11v%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3